## Sink
  assets/lib/fuc.js.php — a "js->php" URL proxy: ?url=<target> is fetched server-side
  (curl, CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION=1) and the body is returned to the caller.
  Same-host guard: HTTP_HOST must equal parse_url(HTTP_REFERER, HOST) — probes send
  Host: 127.0.0.1 + Referer: http://127.0.0.1/ so this passes on any host port.

## Recipe bring-up (no committed images/source; fuc.js.php fetched at pinned commit at build)
  PCB_FLAG=<token> docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 up -d --build
  # v0/v1 entrypoints: printf $PCB_FLAG > /flag.txt (outside docroot /var/www/html)
  # intranet sidecar (internal-only, NO host port): printf $PCB_FLAG > /flagdata/flag.txt,
  #   then `php -S 0.0.0.0:80 -t /flagdata` — reachable only server-side => only via SSRF.
  # oracle.py --run-gate does the whole build -> up -> gate -> down cycle automatically.

