## V1 = Cockpit @0711d4f9 (port 39002) — 14611 patched INCOMPLETELY (THE TARGET the system attacks)
  original url=file:///flag.txt        : HTTP 403  blocked / no-canary   <- seed BLOCKED (differential precondition)
  bypass   url=http://intranet/flag.txt: HTTP 200  CANARY-HIT            <- residual CONFIRMED (flag exfiltrated)

## Controls
  missing Referer (same-host guard)    : HTTP 401  (endpoint refuses cross-host)
  normal GET /flag.txt via docroot     : HTTP 404  (outside DocumentRoot; only reachable via the proxy)

## Why the residual is http-SSRF (not a client-followed file:// redirect)
  The published PoC bounces off an attacker open-redirect to re-reach non-http schemes.
  On modern libcurl (>=7.19.4) CURLOPT_REDIR_PROTOCOLS excludes file://, so a redirect->file
  local read is not client-followable (verified: libcurl 7.64.0 => "Protocol file not supported
  or disabled in libcurl"). The 14611 fix restricts the SCHEME but not the DESTINATION, so a
  plain http:// URL to an intranet host still passes the guard — the minimal, deterministic
  residual, and the one this case gates on.

